1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 a6 4. Ba4 Nf6 5. Qe2 b5 6. Bb3 Bc5 7. a4 Rb8 8. axb5 axb5 9. c3 d6 10. O-O O-O 11. d3 Bd7 12. Bg5 h6 13. Be3 Qc8 14. d4 Bb6 15. Nbd2 Re8 16. Qd3 Qb7 17. h3 Ra8 18. Rxa8 Rxa8 19. dxe5 Nxe5 20. Nxe5 dxe5 21. Bxh6 gxh6 22. Qg3+ Kf8 23. Qxe5 Kg7 24. Qg3+ Kf8 25. Qh4 Kg7 26. e5 Nd5 27. Ne4 Be6 28. Nf6 c6 29. Rd1 Rd8 30. Rd3 Bf5 31. Rg3+ ({Post mortem analysis revealed the following continuation:} 31. Nxd5 Bxd3 ({if} 31... cxd5 32. Qf6+ {wins the bishop}) 32. Nxb6 Qxb6 (32... Re8 33. Qf6+ Kg8 34. e6 fxe6 35. Bxe6+ Kh7 36. Nd7 {wins}) 33. Qf6+ Kg8 34. Qxf7+ Kh8 35. e6 Qb8 ({Stockfish 16:} 35... Ra8 $1 36. e7 $16) 36. e7 Re8 37. Qf6+ Kh7 38. Bf7 {with, it was thought, a win for White. But we are not so sure: cannot Black disentangle himself with} Qc8 {(BHW puts Q-Q2 but this is illegal) answering} 39. Bxe8 (39. Bh5 {wins against this, but wouldn't had BHW's move Qd7 been legal!}) 39... Qxe8 40. Qf8 {with} Bg6 {BH Wood in CHESS}) 31... Bg6 32. Bxd5 cxd5 33. Ng4 Rh8 34. Qf6+ Kh7 35. Nxh6 Bd8 36. Qf4 Qd7 37. h4 Kg7 38. Nf5+ Kf8 39. Nd4 {Sources: CHESS, April 1961, Vol.26/383-4, p255; John Littlewood collection (Keith Brown)} 1/2-1/2

